{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781476384640,"sessionID":"ses_137bc7233ffe5Qp6x7i47s8Qig","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1DsL1sE6ssYsMKrZcGr292mg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+# Checkpoint 1: Policy Application\n+\n+## Controlling Policy Source\n+\n+- Controlling policy: `current_policy.md`\n+- Current policy date: `2026-04-20`\n+- Trip dates being audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`\n+- Reason this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, and this trip started on `2026-05-08`.\n+- Why it supersedes the stale excerpt: `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated `2026-03-01` and explicitly warns that it may be stale if a newer policy applies. The current policy also states that it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is reimbursable up to `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered lodging nights are `2`, so the maximum reimbursable lodging amount is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day, and alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share tips are reimbursable up to `20%` of the base fare; any amount above that cap is not reimbursable.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+# Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Expense Decisions\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Policy / Receipt Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt. Receipt present. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Optional seat upgrade is not reimbursable without written preapproval. Receipt shows no written preapproval. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging is capped at $220.00 per covered night. With 2 covered nights, max reimbursement is $440.00. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt includes $18.00 of wine. Alcohol is not reimbursable, and the remaining $58.00 food cost is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable. Tip reimbursement is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies expense is $75.00 or more, so a receipt is required. No receipt was provided, so the expense is not reimbursable. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt present, no alcohol noted, and amount is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+# Checkpoint 3: Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+## Totals\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+## Reimbursable Total Arithmetic\n+\n+`$480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+\n+## Expense Groupings\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+## Finance Notes\n+\n+- Total claimed amount across all expenses: `$1,281.00`\n+- Difference between claimed and reimbursable totals: `$1,281.00 - $1,056.00 = $225.00`\n+- Main reductions came from the lodging cap, alcohol exclusion, ride-share tip cap, missing required receipt for supplies, and the non-approved seat upgrade.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@\n+# Checkpoint 1: Policy Application\n+\n+## Controlling Policy Source\n+\n+- Controlling policy: `current_policy.md`\n+- Current policy date: `2026-04-20`\n+- Trip dates being audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`\n+- Reason this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, and this trip started on `2026-05-08`.\n+- Why it supersedes the stale excerpt: `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is dated `2026-03-01` and explicitly warns that it may be stale if a newer policy applies. The current policy also states that it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is reimbursable up to `$220.00` per covered night, including room, tax